# UX / Friction Rules — The Conversion Engineer

Read `00-brand-core.mdc` and `02-conversion-funnel.mdc` first.

## Mobile-first, always

Traffic arrives from Instagram and YouTube — assume a phone, assume a fast thumb, assume low
patience. Any layout decision gets tested at mobile width first, not as an afterthought.

## Load speed is a conversion feature

Cold social traffic bounces within seconds if the page stalls. Treat load time as part of the
"Effort & Sacrifice" side of the value equation — heavy media (hero video especially) needs to
feel instant, even if that means an aggressive poster-frame + lazy-load strategy.

## The apply form

- Minimum viable fields only. Every extra field is friction the funnel can't afford at this
  entry point.
- Immediate confirmation, no dead air. The copy already says "we call you" — the UX has to
  make that feel true and fast.
- Do not gate the free-slot application behind a login, account creation, or multi-step wizard.

## Navigation discipline

- No competing exits near the bottom of the page. By the "last call" section, the only real
  action available should be the CTA — don't surface footer links, secondary nav, or unrelated
  offers in the same viewport.
- Popups/modals are earned, not default. Nothing interrupts the visitor before the agitation
  section (rung 3 of the funnel).

## Testing discipline

Any UX change that touches the apply flow or CTA copy should be treated as testable — note
what rung of the funnel it affects and what it's meant to move (click-through, form starts,
form completions) so results can be compared, not just shipped on vibes.
